      "main_full_manual_read": true,
      "main_manual_observations": [
        "Reviewed catalog state/traits, constructors, lookup, insertion, batch validation, replacement, removal, topology/fingerprint caches and all helpers. Catalog owns neutral DTOs; equality compares entries, ignoring derived caches. Snapshot is not a World generation or external budget certificate.",
        "Single insertion requires already admitted dependencies; batch constructors validate the entire closure. Replacement builds a fresh admitted catalog before assignment. Removal handles absent or ambiguous names and directly dependent blocking, then rebuilds identity/name/cache state. Private visibility is metadata, without access-control enforcement.",
        "Only len/is_empty needed new comments. Actual physical rustfmt required removal of two empty CRLF doc separators; every original nonempty line, existing comment, syntax token, string, export and assertion is preserved."
      ],
